{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some places do not let SSE through: some edge runtimes, some mobile WebViews, or a proxy that strips "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text/event-stream"},{"type":"text","value":". Stream newline-delimited JSON (NDJSON) instead. Each line is one JSON "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-return-ndjson-from-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Return NDJSON from the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrap the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" stream with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toHttpResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To write the response yourself, write each chunk as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify(chunk) + \"\\n\""},{"type":"text","value":" to the response body."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-connect-from-the-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Connect from the client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\"),\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":" takes the same options as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchServerSentEvents"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"url"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchClient"},{"type":"text","value":", and dynamic functions. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./request-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Request Options"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On React Native, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":" with the same server. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./react-native","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"resume-a-dropped-stream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resume a dropped stream"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a durability adapter to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse"},{"type":"text","value":". Then each line becomes an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id, chunk }"},{"type":"text","value":" envelope, and the client can continue a reply:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reconnect."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A dropped connection reconnects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Last-Event-ID"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter removes the replayed chunks that it already has."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"joinRun(runId)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"text","value":" It attaches to a run that already exists."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" handler for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"joinRun"},{"type":"text","value":", with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeHttpResponse"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeHttpResponse,\n  toHttpResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"), messages, threadId, runId });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n  });\n}\n\n// joinRun hits GET ?offset=-1&runId=... (replay only, no messages sent).\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeHttpResponse({ adapter: memoryStream(request) });\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream"},{"type":"text","value":" resumes the same way. The guarantees are the same as "},{"type":"link","href":"./sse#resume-a-dropped-stream","children":[{"type":"text","value":"resumable SSE"}]},{"type":"text","value":", over NDJSON."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a message. Each chunk arrives as one JSON line, and the reply streams into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-return-ndjson-from-the-server","text":"1. Return NDJSON from the server","level":2},{"id":"2-connect-from-the-client","text":"2. Connect from the client","level":2},{"id":"resume-a-dropped-stream","text":"Resume a dropped stream","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSome places do not let SSE through: some edge runtimes, some mobile WebViews, or a proxy that strips `text/event-stream`. Stream newline-delimited JSON (NDJSON) instead. Each line is one JSON `StreamChunk`.\n\n## 1. Return NDJSON from the server\n\nWrap the `chat()` stream with `toHttpResponse()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toHttpResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nTo write the response yourself, write each chunk as `JSON.stringify(chunk) + \"\\n\"` to the response body.\n\n## 2. Connect from the client\n\nPass `fetchHttpStream()` to `useChat`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n```\n\n`fetchHttpStream` takes the same options as `fetchServerSentEvents`: `url`, `headers`, `body`, `fetchClient`, and dynamic functions. See [Request Options](./request-options).\n\nOn React Native, use `xhrHttpStream` with the same server. See [React Native](./react-native).\n\n## Resume a dropped stream\n\nPass a durability adapter to `toHttpResponse`. Then each line becomes an `{ id, chunk }` envelope, and the client can continue a reply:\n\n- **Reconnect.** A dropped connection reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`. The adapter removes the replayed chunks that it already has.\n- **`joinRun(runId)`.** It attaches to a run that already exists.\n\nAdd a `GET` handler for `joinRun`, with `resumeHttpResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeHttpResponse,\n  toHttpResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"), messages, threadId, runId });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n  });\n}\n\n// joinRun hits GET ?offset=-1&runId=... (replay only, no messages sent).\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeHttpResponse({ adapter: memoryStream(request) });\n}\n```\n\n`xhrHttpStream` resumes the same way. The guarantees are the same as [resumable SSE](./sse#resume-a-dropped-stream), over NDJSON.\n\nSend a message. Each chunk arrives as one JSON line, and the reply streams into `messages`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: HTTP Stream\nid: transports-http-stream\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Stream chat chunks as newline-delimited JSON with fetchHttpStream and toHttpResponse when SSE is blocked, and resume a stream after the connection drops.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - http stream\n  - ndjson\n  - newline-delimited json\n  - fetchHttpStream\n  - toHttpResponse\n  - resumeHttpResponse\n---\n\nSome places do not let SSE through: some edge runtimes, some mobile WebViews, or a proxy that strips `text/event-stream`. Stream newline-delimited JSON (NDJSON) instead. Each line is one JSON `StreamChunk`.\n\n## 1. Return NDJSON from the server\n\nWrap the `chat()` stream with `toHttpResponse()`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, chatParamsFromRequest, toHttpResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nTo write the response yourself, write each chunk as `JSON.stringify(chunk) + \"\\n\"` to the response body.\n\n## 2. Connect from the client\n\nPass `fetchHttpStream()` to `useChat`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useChat, fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nconst { messages } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\"),\n});\n```\n\n`fetchHttpStream` takes the same options as `fetchServerSentEvents`: `url`, `headers`, `body`, `fetchClient`, and dynamic functions. See [Request Options](./request-options).\n\nOn React Native, use `xhrHttpStream` with the same server. See [React Native](./react-native).\n\n## Resume a dropped stream\n\nPass a durability adapter to `toHttpResponse`. Then each line becomes an `{ id, chunk }` envelope, and the client can continue a reply:\n\n- **Reconnect.** A dropped connection reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`. The adapter removes the replayed chunks that it already has.\n- **`joinRun(runId)`.** It attaches to a run that already exists.\n\nAdd a `GET` handler for `joinRun`, with `resumeHttpResponse`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeHttpResponse,\n  toHttpResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({ adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"), messages, threadId, runId });\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) },\n  });\n}\n\n// joinRun hits GET ?offset=-1&runId=... (replay only, no messages sent).\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeHttpResponse({ adapter: memoryStream(request) });\n}\n```\n\n`xhrHttpStream` resumes the same way. The guarantees are the same as [resumable SSE](./sse#resume-a-dropped-stream), over NDJSON.\n\nSend a message. Each chunk arrives as one JSON line, and the reply streams into `messages`.\n"}
